{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789485763,"nonce":"hSLFhGayqbwbQw/mQ9MZaRXKVEs=","message":"Status against the title, 2026-09-15, after the seam correction (#2)\nand \"bridge is the runtime\" (caribou.Script withdrawn):\n\n- Tick inside the frame pump: landed. Ash c95ecd4 parks\n  hlp_pump_and_sleep's idle time on the scheduler when tasks are alive,\n  the way hlp_sys_sleep and a Lock wait already did through the seam;\n  caribou b3d0f3a adds the frame fixture and test (a Wren fiber counts\n  between the frames of a loop installed through sys_set_loop). So every\n  wait a Haxe program makes is scheduler time, and no call of the\n  program's own is needed. Event delivery from the program's loop comes\n  with the reactor (a655aa5), which is what raises events from outside.\n- Name-keyed lookup: landed earlier through the registry\n  (Session::call, registry::lookup_class_or_load).\n- Per-world state replacing ash's process globals: not done, and not\n  planned under the seam: ash keeps its globals, one Haxe program per\n  process is the driver (Session is one per process). Recommend dropping.\n- Droppable interpreter: not done. Program leaks after start by design\n  (ash's closure runner and every published callable keep raw pointers\n  into it); nothing frees it because the program is the driver and lives\n  as long as the process. Recommend dropping until something needs a\n  second program in one process.\n- BytecodeDecoder::from_bytes: not done; the bundle (4f07ca7) is its\n  consumer, noted there.\n\nFound on the way: wren_lift 44633bc (a fiber body in a static method\nreads the class's statics as they were when the fiber was made).","files":null}]}